{"skill":{"slug":"audio","displayName":"Audio"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1771173233419,"changelog":"Declare required binaries (ffmpeg, ffprobe), add requirements section with optional deps, add explicit scope","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2870,"sha256":"7d7300fc92ac84fd834e41e6740d2013b31ad84a266b3c7e9872605d4a6ca6a4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"commands.md","size":5754,"sha256":"869e877ae63e0178aa3490431f57645d713b0df7642db905557b46d4332c9e9e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"loudness.md","size":2903,"sha256":"3932f04fd3446c10b7ba1ff64098edd2f64ec5c035ec7840cb4ea76c33b104fc","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"podcast.md","size":3839,"sha256":"f888af3e81752566617523d3ad120f48178232631379f7f47772f6417ff87276","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"transcription.md","size":5061,"sha256":"36d9c49e74aae6d4831276f5ba154e93d1b1b260e77fe58d1324ab62d89f1391","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2374,"sha256":"5698fccd7a00dd1fe08d882d017361e06a81085c840348e13d664d32abc14f7e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789064381727,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"602945d9061471d6999ff3e1573e36627f4e9cdce8114514e3ab6dc7826e1ea5","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/602945d9061471d6999ff3e1573e36627f4e9cdce8114514e3ab6dc7826e1ea5","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: audio\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill bundle is classified as suspicious due to significant shell injection vulnerabilities. Specifically, the use of `ffmpeg -f concat -safe 0` in `commands.md` and `podcast.md` allows arbitrary file paths in the concatenation list, posing a risk if the agent constructs this list from unsanitized user input. Additionally, other shell commands involving command substitution and arithmetic (`$()`, `bc`) in `commands.md` and `podcast.md` could lead to arbitrary code execution if user-provided input is not properly sanitized by the OpenClaw agent before being passed to the shell.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163602405},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":28,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789064381727},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This audio-processing skill is coherent and purpose-aligned, with some ordinary caution needed around optional cloud transcription services, API keys, and unpinned package installs.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The requested environment use is proportionate: local audio files, FFmpeg/ffprobe, optional local transcription tools, and explicit optional API workflows for transcription or diarization.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill documents common pip and conda install commands for optional transcription tools without version pins or hashes. This is common for instructional skills but users should install in an isolated environment and verify package provenance.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The scope says cloud services are not accessed without the user knowing, and the transcription guide labels AssemblyAI and Deepgram as API-based; however, it could more explicitly warn that audio or transcript data may leave the user's environment when API services are used.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No artifact-backed evidence shows persistence, privilege escalation, background services, memory writes, hidden tool modification, destructive behavior, or automatic execution beyond user-directed commands.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill provides Markdown guidance for FFmpeg audio processing, loudness normalization, podcast workflows, and transcription of user-provided audio files; these capabilities match its stated purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, treat cloud transcription as third-party processing of potentially sensitive recordings, keep API tokens out of shell history and source control, and install optional Python/Conda tools in a dedicated virtual environment or container with reviewed package versions where possible.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The privacy concern is valid as guidance: podcast and transcription workflows may involve sensitive audio, but the API options are visibly labeled as API-based and remain purpose-aligned.\n[E1] expected: The AssemblyAI endpoint is an explicit optional transcription example, not hidden exfiltration; users should understand that using it sends data or an audio URL to a third-party provider.\n[SQP-2] expected: The token examples use placeholders, but the skill would be clearer if it recommended environment variables or secret managers for API and Hugging Face tokens.\n[T08] expected: The unpinned package install commands are security-relevant but are disclosed setup instructions for optional audio/transcription tools, not evidence of malicious dependency behavior in the artifact.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789064381727}}}}}